Z||000002||p4n1c||05-03-2001||08:26 AM||||Thanks for the info, I looked at the Fiero one and it was for an engine without an A/C.  I looked at the W-Body page, but the one they have listed is for the 91-96 3.4 DOHC.<P>Dad told me he'd give me the '88 Cutlass they have.  So I'm looking for performance options.  The engine right now has 402,000kms on it.  The only problem with it is the transmission is starting to show it's age and needs to be rebuilt or replaced(which he is looking into), the engine is still very mechanically sound.  I still haven't decided if I want to take the car, but free car + cheaper insurance = good.<P>I wonder if a 3.4 DOHC swap would work down the road when the engine finally puts out it's lost growl.  I know the 91+ Cutlass Internationals have it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||05-05-2001||02:22 AM||||I dropped a 3800SC into my Ciera GT. That's probably an easier swap overall.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Predator||05-05-2001||10:01 AM||||From what I have seen there is not a super charger made for the 2.8 that can have the AC attached. That's why a lot of people especially in the South opt for the Turbo system instead.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||p4n1c||05-05-2001||11:20 AM||||Thanks for all the info.  I guess I'll either save up and get the engine rebuilt for adding a turbo(it has aluminum heads and I though I heard somewhere that they don't last very long with a turbo, correct me if I'm wrong) or go for an engine swap.<P>I mentioned swapping in the 3.4 DOHC because of the '91+ Cutlass Supremes Int. having them, I just thought it might be a straight forward swap, I'll look into seeing if they totally redesigned the engine mounts and everything else for that year.<P>Thanks again.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 05-05-2001).]||||reg||1
